  "id": "BIT-mongodb-2026-8843",
  "summary": "Calling createIndex with certain index types can crash mongod",
  "details": "Creating a \"2dsphere_bucket\" index on a non-timeseries bucket collection will succeed, but any subsequent attempt to insert a document which triggers updating that index will crash the server. A similar issue occurs when creating \"queryable_encrypted_range\" indices.\n\nThis issue affects MongoDB Server v7.0 versions prior to 7.0.32, v8.0 versions prior to 8.0.21 and v8.2 versions prior to 8.2.6",
